{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Convert each decodable file listed in encodings.tsv into normalized/ under the matching filename, using UTF-8 and LF line endings while preserving accented characters, empty records, and whether the source ended with a newline.","status":"satisfied","summary":"western.txt and utf8.txt were published under matching names. Direct byte inspection shows valid UTF-8 accents, LF-only endings, the empty western.txt record, a trailing LF for western.txt, and no trailing LF for utf8.txt. The same bytes survived restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8bd79bddcb84e6a","cmd-55bfd5fe7bd34c15","cmd-aa96f03cabf24f00","cmd-e130ccfc4d52446d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Report undecodable input without replacing invalid characters or publishing a partial output.","status":"satisfied","summary":"invalid.txt contains an invalid FF byte under its declared UTF-8 encoding. The final lossless conversion reported it as undecodable/lossy, removed any destination, and final checks before and after restart showed exactly two outputs with invalid.txt absent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c8bd79bddcb84e6a","cmd-55bfd5fe7bd34c15","cmd-aa96f03cabf24f00","cmd-e130ccfc4d52446d"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep all source files in /srv/legacy2/text-export-normalization intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three incoming files retained their preparation-baseline SHA-256 hashes before publication and after restart. The complete trace contains no write to encodings.tsv, whose contents were read consistently during processing.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-229e1521c4354bdf","cmd-aa96f03cabf24f00","cmd-e130ccfc4d52446d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts before and after execution and restart. Processing used already-installed Alpine/BusyBox-compatible utilities, with no package installation or OS mutation shown.","evidence_ids":["cmd-229e1521c4354bdf","cmd-aa96f03cabf24f00","cmd-e130ccfc4d52446d","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"The required final state is clean and package health and network exposure show no adverse executor-caused change. One unnecessary transient mutation occurred: cmd-788c4cd6bf144c6c incorrectly published invalid.txt after the platform iconv silently dropped FF; this was fully reverted by cmd-55bfd5fe7bd34c15, which removed that destination and atomically republished the valid files. The mandatory restart command also left the small /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log artifact behind; it remained after execution. Other mutations—creating normalized/, publishing the two valid results, temporary-file cleanup, and rebooting—had clear task or restart-evidence roles.","evidence_ids":["cmd-788c4cd6bf144c6c","cmd-55bfd5fe7bd34c15","cmd-cb30cf4ca5504afa","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, connectivity was observably interrupted, a different boot ID appeared, and source/output integrity and platform state were revalidated. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["No final checksum was captured for encodings.tsv itself; its intactness is inferred from the complete command timeline showing it only being read, while all incoming source files were directly hash-verified.","Alpine does not provide the collector's systemd failed-unit check. Recovery is nevertheless directly supported by successful post-restart access, restored SSH listening state, unchanged platform observations, and complete file validation."]}
